// V6 task 5 (FORMAL_VERIFICATION.md): the CONTRACT-LESS degrade rule.
// `plain_read` carries no requires/ensures/decreases; its body reads a
// struct field — outside the verifiable subset — so the walk fails the
// subset. Since task 5 that report DEGRADES to the passing
// `outside-subset` outcome for contract-less fns (infrastructure,
// nothing was promised), instead of a subset ERROR: `yo verify` over a
// raw-pointer module goes green with honest per-fn notes, while a
// CONTRACTED fn with the same body (or `assumed()`) is the loud path.
// Needs no solver — the walk rejects the body before any obligation.
pragma(Pragma.Verify);

Holder :: ref(
  struct(
    _v : i32
  )
);

plain_read :: (fn(h : Holder) -> (r : i32))(h._v);
